id: pm-rbcvt2
title: "Reproducible workspace instances: seeded identifiers, injectable clock, and byte-identical construction from a declared recipe"
description: "Two runs of the same script against a fresh pm workspace produce different data. Identifiers are random, timestamps are wall-clock, and history entry hashes chain over both, so nothing downstream of a workspace can be compared byte for byte across runs. That blocks four things at once: golden-file testing of anything that emits ids or times, reproducible benchmark corpora at the scales the scale-out programme targets, deterministic training and evaluation episodes, and the strongest form of the reconstruction guarantee, namely that a recorded stream replays to a bit-identical workspace on a different machine years later. The primitive is small and self-contained: allow a workspace to be constructed with a declared seed and a declared clock so that identifier generation and timestamping become pure functions of the recipe, and make the recipe itself a recorded artifact. Determinism is opt-in and off by default, so real tracking is unaffected. Fences: pm-a8lnoh owns seeded interleavings for testing pm's own races and would consume this rather than duplicate it; pm-wlqxg3 owns proving that an existing stream replays to the recorded state, which is replay of real history rather than construction from a seed; pm-z71aoy needs representative corpora and is the immediate beneficiary; pm-khdq is the identifier allocation race, which is a correctness bug in the current generator rather than a determinism feature."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[6]: "area:storage",determinism,reproducibility,rl,storage,testing
created_at: "2026-07-26T22:04:50.255Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T16:31:05.088Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T16:28:18.073Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "A workspace can be constructed from a declared recipe consisting of a seed, a clock and an operation sequence, and two constructions from the same recipe are byte-identical including identifiers, timestamps and history hashes; determinism is opt-in and the default behaviour of real workspaces is unchanged; the recipe is a first-class artifact that can be stored, shared and re-executed by a different machine and a different pm build within the supported format window; the benchmark and token-budget corpora are generated from recipes rather than committed fixtures; the deterministic path is exercised in CI, and a deliberate nondeterminism regression fails it; the clock injection is total, so no code path reads wall-clock time directly when a clock is supplied"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: implemented
expected_result: "A versioned seed, clock, and operation recipe constructs identical authoritative workspace bytes when explicitly enabled."
actual_result: Real SDK create sequences in independent initialized roots now yield identical content-addressed snapshot fingerprints.
